From 138b6b6c30856bf0c806d7bc7985e142c0e41cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:28:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] hostgap: sync-free FlashInfer plan for EAGLE target
 verify

FlashInfer's BatchPrefillWithPagedKVCacheWrapper.plan blocks the host four
times per EAGLE verify replay: segment_packbits sizes the packed custom
mask with .item(), then qo_indptr, paged_kv_indptr and last_page_len are
read back with .to("cpu"). Each read waits for the draft graph, so the
host plans while the GPU idles. Every value they return follows from the
batch's seq_lens_cpu and draft_token_num, which the host already holds.

SGLANG_HOSTGAP_VERIFY_PLAN=1 swaps fast_verify_plan onto the CUDA-graph
verify wrappers at their first replay (capture-time plans stay stock). It
mirrors plan() step by step for the fa2 backend with those values computed
on the host, so plan_info, the pinned plan bytes and every device buffer
the graph reads are the ones plan() would produce. A per-wrapper event
orders reuse of the pinned plan buffer after its previous copy, which the
stock blocking reads used to guarantee (also for the draft-extend
wrapper's fast_prefill_plan). SGLANG_HOSTGAP_VALIDATE=1 runs the stock
plan alongside and raises on any difference. Both flags default to off.
